course: dictionary
lesson: 14148
title: When a name is wrong
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A misnomer is a name or word that is wrong or misleading for the thing it describes. The word starts with mis-, which means wrong, so a misnomer is a name that gets it wrong.
explain: «A jellyfish is not a fish.» The name suggests fish, but it is not one, so jellyfish is a misnomer. A starfish is not a fish either, and «koala bears» are not bears, so those names are misnomers too.
explain: To spot a misnomer, ask: does this name tell the truth about the thing? If the name is wrong or misleading, you have found one. People often say «a bit of a misnomer» or «a well-known misnomer».
fact: A misnomer is a name that is wrong or misleading for the thing it describes.
fact: «A jellyfish is not a fish», so the name jellyfish is a misnomer.
fact: «Peanuts are not nuts»: they are legumes, so the name peanut is a misnomer.
fact: «Lead pencils» contain graphite, not lead, so that name is a misnomer too.
fact: Misnomers are used in phrases like «a bit of a misnomer» and «a well-known misnomer».
exercise: «A starfish is not a fish, so its name is a misnomer.» What is a misnomer? | A kind of fish | A word that means the same as fish | A name that is very long | *A name that is wrong or misleading for the thing it describes
exercise: Which of these is a misnomer? | Sunflower | *Lead pencil, which contains graphite and no lead | Rainbow | Apple
exercise: Bob is called «Tiny», but he is the tallest in class. What is the name Tiny for Bob? | A name meaning very small, so it is correct | A nickname for a dog | *A misnomer, because the name is wrong for him | A name from the dictionary
test: What does a misnomer tell you about a name? | It is always spelt with two letters | It is always rude | *It is wrong or misleading | It is a rhyme
test: Which sentence uses misnomer correctly? | «The sun is a misnomer, because it is a very long word.» | «Please pass me a misnomer for my tea.» | *«The jellyfish is a well-known misnomer, because it is not a fish.»
exam: Why is «starfish» a misnomer? | Because it lives in the sky | *Because it is not a fish | Because it is always blue | Because it is a kind of star
